  "final_message": "I wrote `answer.json` with four functions whose own code emits `subscription.updated`:\n\n- `subscriptions.transition` emits it for every status change except a move to `canceled`, which emits `subscription.canceled` instead.\n- `subscriptions.change_items` emits it after the subscription's items are replaced.\n- `subscriptions.cancel` emits it when cancellation is scheduled for period end.\n- `subscriptions.reactivate` emits it when a scheduled cancellation is undone.\n\n`pause`, `resume` and the other callers of `transition` only reach the event through it, so they aren't listed. No other module in `billing` emits that event type. I found this by searching with grep and reading the emit calls, and I didn't run the tests.",
